Short:        Two-pane file manager for AmigaOS 4
Author:       vagappc
Uploader:     vagappc
Type:         util/dir
Version:      1.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition, ReAction
Architecture: ppc-amigaos >= 4.1
Date:         22-Nov-2026
Distribution: Aminet

VagaFileManager 1.0 build 16
============================

VagaFileManager (VFM) is a two-pane file manager for AmigaOS 4.1 built
with ReAction/BOOPSI.  It is intended for users who prefer a fast,
keyboard-friendly directory browser to dozens of Workbench windows.

Main features
-------------
- Single-pane or split two-pane browsing.
- Icon view and detailed list view (name, type, size, date).
- Dynamic toolbar: the available actions follow the current selection.
- Copy, move, duplicate, rename and recursive delete.
- Conflict handling with Overwrite / Overwrite all / Update / Update all /
  Rename / Skip.
- Progress window with file count, transferred size and percentage;
  cancel and pause/resume.
- Recursive size calculation with an animated activity bar.
- Drag and drop: move on the same device, copy across devices; multiple
  selection is supported.
- Quick filter with AmigaDOS wildcards (#?, ?, [], ~, *) or plain text.
- Recursive Find with a results window and AmigaDOS wildcards; selecting a
  result reveals the file in the active pane.
- Bookmarks, history navigation, root/volume view.
- Per-volume window size and position; navigation does not resize the
  window.
- "Open" on a drawer opens a new VFM instance centered on the pointer;
  double-click navigates in the current window.
- Optional Workbench drawer-window replacement (WB2VagaFileManager).
- Built-in ARexx port (VAGAFILEMANAGER) and Python plugin support.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition.
- ReAction classes (window.class, layout.gadget, button.gadget,
  string.gadget, listbrowser.gadget) included in AmigaOS 4.1 FE.
- Python is optional and only needed for Python plugins (C:Python or
  C:Python3).  ARexx plugins use C:RX.

Installation
------------
1. Copy the VFM drawer and VFM.info together to a location of your choice,
   for example Work:Utilities/.
2. Keep the drawer structure intact:
     VFM/VagaFileManager
     VFM/WB2VagaFileManager
     VFM/icons/
     VFM/Catalogs/
     VFM/Plugins/
3. Start VFM/VagaFileManager.  The drawer icon is VFM.info.

Catalogs
--------
English is the built-in fallback.  The Amiga release build includes
catalogs for English, Italian, French, German, Polish and Spanish under
Catalogs/<language>/VagaFileManager.catalog.  A cross-built test archive
may not contain them; catalogs are optional and the program falls back to
the built-in English strings when a catalog is missing.

Plugins
-------
Scripts are read from VFM/Plugins.  After copying a .py or .rexx file,
use "Scripts -> Refresh" in VFM and select it from the menu.

The included ARexxDemo.py shows a Python addon with a real Reaction
dialog.  It uses the VFM --dialog file API, so the window does not depend
on the Python arexx module:
    VagaFileManager --dialog "@T:specfile"

Python addons can also control VFM through a file-based command channel:
they write a one-line request in their channel directory, run
`VagaFileManager --notify <drop-port>` and read the reply.  The commands
are the same as the ARexx API (CD, PATH, ENTRIES, SELECTED, DIALOG, ...).
This works even when the system ARexx/RX host lookup is not working; the
addon keeps a C:RX fallback for older VFM builds.

The ARexx port is public and named VAGAFILEMANAGER (a suffixed name is
used when several instances are running).  Typical commands are CD, OPEN,
UP, REFRESH, PATH, ENTRIES, SELECTED, REVEAL, SIZE, VIEW, SORT, MODE and
SCRIPT.  Send VERSION for the program version.

Notes
-----
- The old name of the distribution drawer was VMF.  Starting with build 9
  the drawer is called VFM (Vaga File Manager).  Remove the old VMF
  drawer to avoid starting an old copy by mistake.
- The optional WB2VagaFileManager is a commodity/drawer patch; read its
  tooltypes and test it on a copy of your Workbench setup first.
- Window geometry is stored in ENVARC:VagaFileManager.prefs, separately
  per volume.  Bookmarks are in ENVARC:VagaFileManager.bookmarks.

Changes in build 16
-------------------
- Quick filter: 300 ms debounce, so the directory is not re-read on every
  keystroke; the list updates as soon as typing pauses.
- Find: patterns without wildcards use the fast substring search again;
  the dos.library pattern matcher is used only when wildcards are present.

Changes in build 15
-------------------
- Find accepts AmigaDOS wildcards (#?, ?, [], ~) and * in the search
  pattern; a pattern without wildcards remains a substring match.

Changes in build 14
-------------------
- Find.py rewritten for the file-based plugin channel.  It asks for the
  pattern, searches recursively from the active pane, shows the results
  in a listbrowser and reveals the selected file.
- The Find/Grep results window now returns the selected row; Find
  navigates to the drawer and selects the file.
- Added CHANGELOG.md.

Changes in build 13
-------------------
- The quick filter is applied in real time while typing; Enter is no
  longer required.

Changes in build 12
-------------------
- Plugin file channel: the synthetic RexxMsg now sets RXFF_RESULT, so
  VERSION, PATH, ENTRIES, SELECTED and the other query commands return
  their text instead of an empty string.

Changes in build 11
-------------------
- Python plugins: new file-based command channel (req_/rep_ files plus
  `VagaFileManager --notify`), so CD, PATH, ENTRIES, SELECTED, DIALOG and
  the other commands work without ARexx/RX.
- ARexxDemo.py uses the channel for commands and keeps the C:RX fallback.

Changes in build 10
-------------------
- Root view: DELETE and Copy/Move no longer act on a whole volume or
  assign; the path gadget has its own buffer and LoadPath works on a copy.
- Cancelling a move no longer deletes the source (partial copies and
  read errors are reported as failures).
- Drag&drop rejects file names with C0/C1 control characters, so a name
  containing Return cannot run commands in a Shell.
- Recursive copy/delete/count use heap buffers and a 256-level limit;
  copying a deep drawer tree no longer overflows the stack.  A move does
  not delete the source when the copy fails.

Changes in build 9
------------------
- Distribution drawer renamed from VMF to VFM (VFM.info).
- Added the Aminet/OS4Depot readme.
- WB2 version string now uses the shared version date.

